## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical integration of OpenAI with security tooling, automation, and multi-tenant isolation, plus safety controls (PII redaction, auditing) and deployment practices (canary rollout).

## Key Concepts
- OpenAI integration with Defender for Cloud and CI/CD tooling
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search on Azure Blob
- Per-tenant state in Cosmos DB; secret management via Key Vault
- Azure Automation or IaC task generation for remediation
- PII redaction, Data Lake auditing, API Management canary

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: ingest alerts, ground to KB, generate remediation, dispatch runbook
async function handleIncident(tenantId, alert) {
  const kb = await loadKB(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(alert, kb);
  const guidance = await openai.complete(prompt);
  if (validate(guidance)) {
    const runbook = generateRunbook(guidance);
    await dispatchRunbook(runbook, tenantId);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollout and measure safety/latency impact?
- What failure modes require fallback behavior and how would you implement it?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design end-to-end Azure OpenAI-powered data-governance tooling that handles multi-tenant isolation, secure KB grounding, and robust testing.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage ingestion and normalization across Synapse/Data Factory.
- Versioned KB in Azure Blob and Cognitive Search integration.
- Per-tenant isolation with Key Vault-backed Cosmos DB storage.
- Prompt engineering with fallback chains and confidence scoring.
- Data redaction and auditability.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for gap-filling using KB
async function fillLineageGap(partialLineage, kbClient) {
  if (partialLineage.isComplete()) return partialLineage;
  const kb = await kbClient.query(partialLineage.pattern);
  return partialLineage.enrich(kb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure the accuracy of enrichment?
- How would you handle cycles or conflicting KB results?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes real-world design for geo-distributed, policy-driven AI helpers with strong data governance and canary controls.

## Key Concepts
- Regional OpenAI inference and API Management orchestration
- Per-tenant policy engine (PII, residency) in Cosmos
- Canary rollout governance and feature flags
- PII redaction with Text Analytics and privacy-by-design
- KB grounding with Cognitive Search; audit logging to Data Lake
- Secrets management with Key Vault; end‑to‑end telemetry with Monitor

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: select region, validate tenant policy, route to OpenAI, redact PII in response
function handleRequest(req){
  const tenant=req.headers['x-tenant'];
  if(!policyOk(tenant, req.body)) throw new Error('Policy violation');
  const region=regionForTenant(tenant);
  const resp=openAiCall(req.body, region);
  return redact(resp, tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test canary rollout safety and rollback speed?
- How would you enforce cross-region data residency and minimize latency?

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to translate regulatory requirements into automated, auditable technical controls using Azure AI and governance services, with strict multi-tenant isolation requirements.

## Key Concepts

- Regulatory-to-controls mapping (GDPR/CCPA/NIST)
- Knowledge base grounding with Cognitive Search
- Per-tenant RBAC and data isolation
- Automated evidence collection and auditable logging
- Azure Policy integration for continuous enforcement

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: Map obligations to controls and enforce per-tenant policy
async function ensureCompliance(clientId) {
  const obligations = await kb.fetchObligations(clientId);
  const controls = await mapToControls(obligations);

  const evidence = await collectEvidence(clientId, controls);
  const violations = await evaluateAgainstPolicy(controls, evidence);

  await logDecision({ clientId, obligations, controls, evidence, violations });
  return generateRemediationPlan(violations);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to design scalable, compliant, multi-tenant AI flows in Azure, balancing data residency, prompt governance, and cost.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant data residency and isolation
- Prompt versioning and policy gating
- Pluggable grounding knowledge sources
- Canary-style prompt rollouts behind API Management
- Prompt caching and cost controls
- Auditing and telemetry across tenants

